        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John O'Hara, Bobbie Ann Mason\n- Works: Elizabeth Appleton\n- Topics: American literature, social realism\n\nFacts:\n- John O'Hara was born on January 31, 1905, and he died on April 11, 1970.\n- John O'Hara was an American writer known for observing social status and manners in early- to mid-20th-century America.\n- John O'Hara was regarded as pre-eminent among his contemporaries in depicting social realism.\n- Bobbie Ann Mason was born on May 1, 1940.\n- Bobbie Ann Mason is a Southern United States novelist, short story writer, essayist, and literary critic from Kentucky.\n- Elizabeth Appleton is a novel by John O'Hara that was first published in 1963.",
